id: pm-runner-qualification-delivery
title: Preserve fail-closed startup benchmark runner qualification and complete diagnostics
description: Bounded execution child of pm-bj7rq0 for bracketed bare-process controls and retained admission evidence. Deliver portable runner observations and explicit unsuccessful unqualified admission while preserving every existing product latency and RSS ceiling. The parent retains historical root-cause diagnosis and is not completed by this task.
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-10T19:33:27.145Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-11T02:27:12.157Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-11T02:27:11.558Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-11T02:27:11.558Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: Both SDK and CLI gates bracket their measurements with warmed bare-process controls and portable environment evidence; over-budget or missing controls fail with product admission unverified and retain the full report; qualified product regressions still fail and retain all violations; positive and negative controls pass without any product budget increase; public methodology and linked evidence document the historical diagnosis boundary.
value: Context management needs trustworthy performance evidence that separates observed runner qualification from product admission.
parent: pm-bj7rq0
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: Bracketed SDK/CLI measurements with complete runner diagnostics and prior-policy qualification before calibration; SDK updates also compare the proposed p95-derived control ceiling with the existing ceiling and refuse any increase before mkdir or writes. Existing committed control/product budgets and calibrated performance tables remain unchanged.
expected_result: Both controls must qualify and a proposed control ceiling must be equal or lower before calibration writes; refused runs retain measurements and preserve original budget and documentation bytes.
actual_result: "The pre-fix p50=42/p95=999 case writes a raised ceiling and fails the negative regression; current 36 linked runner tests pass, preserving bytes and accepting an equal ceiling. Full static/typecheck and serialized nine-package npm/Bun/SDK acceptance pass; final-head hosted checks and renewed full review remain mandatory."
comments[11]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-10T19:33:27.145Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete 2920-item strict all-status census plus request-specific search and open/in-progress inventories found only canonical diagnosis pm-bj7rq0 and no focused execution child. Existing implementation is already owned and claimed under that diagnosis. This child records its independently complete qualification delivery so the generated changelog reports shipped tooling without closing an unproven historical cause."
  "2026-10-10T19:37:23.079Z","harness:codex","Final verification includes 27 benchmark tests plus the unchanged-base runtime comparison. Node26 observations include an unqualified control refusal during load and a separate qualified merge-entrypoint overrun (241 ms against226 ms), which is retained rather than treated as a pass. The SDK measurement recovery no longer imports Commander registration after pure argv extraction; focused144-test verification and typechecking pass. The historical diagnosis remains owned by pm-bj7rq0."
  "2026-10-10T19:50:51.653Z","harness:codex","Reviewed delivery: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1436 includes both bracketed startup gates, complete fail-closed reports, portable methodology, 27 linked tests and this bounded closure. Initial source commit a279913ba retains all budgets; real Node24 gates pass. Historical cause diagnosis remains open under the parent. Final-head CI and review are required before merge; the latest published changelog generator checked the Unreleased entry."
  "2026-10-10T22:18:25.834Z","harness:codex","PR #1436 final-head review https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1436#pullrequestreview-5480989632: A rejected final bare-Node control currently rejects the report builder after product measurements, losing completed diagnostics. Capture unavailable final-control evidence and preserve unsuccessful product admission."
  "2026-10-10T22:50:36.497Z","harness:codex","Final-control review remediation: both benchmark builders retain every completed operation or entrypoint when the final bare-Node control rejects, recording unavailable status and the original diagnostic. Check admission remains unsuccessful and unqualified with product admission unverified, while preserving product violations; calibration refuses before rewriting existing budget or documentation files. Error and string-rejection regressions pass for both builders. All 31 linked runner tests pass; real SDK and CLI benchmark gates qualify this runner and pass unchanged latency/RSS/30ms-control margins. Typecheck and all static gates pass, including zero duplicated blocks and mutation audit 336 total / 329 killed / 7 verified equivalent / 0 failures. Historical startup-cause attribution remains in the open parent lineage."
  "2026-10-11T01:22:17.899Z","harness:codex","Full review b6af17a4-5495-4dbf-af35-c25e096af957 covers base c233923 through 1cd68972a and identifies an update-mode admission gap: current guards reject unavailable final controls but permit available controls above the existing ceiling. Reopened and claimed only this runner delivery for real before/after calibration preservation tests and qualification before writes; no committed latency/RSS/control ratchets will be raised."
  "2026-10-11T01:25:41.304Z","harness:codex","Independent pre-fix negatives fail for both baseline and baseline_after over-budget controls in SDK and CLI update mode (four real calibration-writing regressions). Current repaired command tests reject before writing and preserve existing JSON budgets and documentation byte-for-byte. SDK admission loads the existing target policy, or committed control policy for a new target; CLI uses the SDK control budget. Both controls must qualify before mkdir or writes. Missing/malformed policy remains fail-closed. No committed budget or performance documentation calibration value was modified."
  "2026-10-11T01:40:03.697Z","harness:codex","Final review remediation verification: four pre-fix calibration negatives fail as expected; current 35 runner regressions pass, including valid high-p95 SDK controls and byte-for-byte preservation of existing calibration targets. Existing full static/typecheck and final delta lint pass without altered ratchets. Current serialized packed nine-package npm/npx/Bun/bunx/SDK acceptance passes. Committed SDK/CLI budget JSON and calibrated performance tables have no diff. Fresh next-head CI and renewed full review remain mandatory."
  "2026-10-11T02:14:10.471Z","harness:codex","PR #1436 full review at b07c19d3853d1cc60a12e61d7cf7e6b4ce4d6d88, https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1436#discussion_r4239948593: p50=42 qualifies against a 60ms control ceiling while p95=999 proposes 1349ms. Reopen only this delivery owner, prove the pre-fix write, and refuse an increased proposed control ceiling before calibration writes; retain all measurements and unchanged committed ratchets."
  "2026-10-11T02:15:52.458Z","harness:codex","Independent pre-fix regression reproduces a qualified p50=42/p95=999 update writing an increased control ceiling; current focused run passes. Update now builds proposed budgets once and refuses any increased baseline ceiling against existing policy before mkdir/writes, using complete qualified failure diagnostics. Existing calibration bytes and documentation remain unchanged on refusal; an equal-ceiling update remains accepted. No committed budget JSON or calibrated table changes."
  "2026-10-11T02:27:10.886Z","harness:codex","Final local remediation receipts: real pre-fix qualified-control inflation fails, while the corrected 36 runner regressions and immutable linked recording pass. The full static pipeline and typecheck pass, including unchanged startup controls/product budgets, dependency/secret/contract/record gates and 329 killed plus 7 recognized equivalent mutations. Serialized nine-package npm/npx/Bun/bunx and SDK consumers pass. Higher proposed control ceilings refuse before mkdir/writes; existing budgets/docs are preserved and equal ceilings remain accepted. Fresh next-head CI and full review are required before merge."
